            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac{49}{100}$",
              "worked": "The fair- and brown-hair categories are mutually exclusive.\n$$\\begin{align*}n(\\text{fair hair})&=25+16+15=56\\\\n(\\text{brown hair})&=9+16+17=42\\\\P(\\text{fair or brown hair})&=\\frac{56+42}{200}\\\\P(\\text{fair or brown hair})&=\\frac{49}{100}\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 32
          },
          {
            "id": "p13-q8-d",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "d",
            "prompt": "blue or brown eyes?",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac{13}{20}$",
              "worked": "The blue- and brown-eye categories are mutually exclusive.\n$$\\begin{align*}n(\\text{blue eyes})&=25+9+6+18=58\\\\n(\\text{brown eyes})&=16+16+18+22=72\\\\P(\\text{blue or brown eyes})&=\\frac{58+72}{200}\\\\P(\\text{blue or brown eyes})&=\\frac{13}{20}\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 32
